224-/**
225- * Send an email. Never throws — logs and returns false on failure so callers
226- * don't break flows. EVERY attempt is written to `EmailLog` (SENT on success,
227- * FAILED + error otherwise) for the admin Logs viewer.
228- *
229- * NOTIFICATION PREFERENCES are enforced HERE, not at the call sites.
230- * `User.notificationPrefs` was a column the customer edited and nothing read, so
231- * turning off "email me about billing" changed nothing. Gating each send site
232- * individually would have fixed today's sites and left every future one to
233- * re-introduce the bug; gating centrally means a new send site inherits the
234- * policy automatically and per-site checks become defence in depth.
235- *
236- * Two deliberate properties, both fail-open:
237- *   - no `kind` (or no `userId`) → send. Unclassified is never silenced.
238- *   - `mayDeliverTo` returns true for anything non-suppressible without touching
239- *     the database, and also on a lookup error. A payment-failure or suspension
240- *     warning must not be lost because a preference read failed.
